From: Vladimir Skvortsov <vskvortsov@emcraft.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 13:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] iot_ab: do not require EFI capsule support

The A/B boot code reads and writes the boot-control record on the
"misc" partition and uses no EFI service, but its option depends on
EFI_HAVE_CAPSULE_SUPPORT. With the EFI loader disabled the option is
dropped silently and U-Boot never marks the booted slot good.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Vladimir Skvortsov <vskvortsov@emcraft.com>
---
--- a/boot/Kconfig
+++ b/boot/Kconfig
@@ -1388,6 +1388,5 @@
 config MEDIATEK_IOT_AB_BOOT_SUPPORT
 	bool "MediaTek IoT Yocto A/B updates"
-	depends on EFI_HAVE_CAPSULE_SUPPORT
 	help
 	  Add support for MediaTek IoT Yocto A/B updates. This allows the bootloader
 	  to select which slot to boot from based on the information provided by
